<title>KENYA: Prices generally down at Mombasa tea auction.</title>
<headline>Prices generally down at Mombasa tea auction.</headline>
<dateline>MOMBASA, Kenya 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices for Kenyan tea were generally down at the weekly tea auction in Mombasa on Monday, auction officials said.</p>
<p>Brighter and medium BP1s were generally easier by 3-8 U.S. cents, while lower mediums appreciated up to four cents. Brighter and medium Pdusts were a little irregular while lower mediums fell by up to two cents.</p>
<p>Pakistan was forceful. There was strong inquiry from Egypt.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261</p>
</text>
